    delphi:hasConfidence "0.78"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Whole-domain concordance versus cell-independent mosaics gives a clear statistical test. Published evidence can test the phenomenon in selected systems, but the decision interpretation and cross-system generalization remain partly confounded." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Use spatial single-embryo outcome maps to compare observed within-domain concordance of left-right identity or melanocyte conversion with an independent-cell Bernoulli model, accounting for lineage and shared exposure." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Raw spatial cell-level outcomes may not be deposited.", "Shared upstream signals can coordinate outcomes without a domain-level decision process." .
